# Mezo Development Kit — Manifest v1.4.0

**Status:** Accepted project baseline

**Released:** 2026-09-24

**Improvement log:** [Manifest changelog](./manifest-changelog.md)

## Purpose and scope

Mezo Developer Kit (MDK) helps developers build on Mezo through composable
TypeScript packages, evidence-backed protocol knowledge, practical examples,
and portable coding-agent guidance. Its architecture makes correct behavior
understandable, testable, and reusable.

The current distribution is an experimental GitHub source alpha with private
workspace packages and a private packed-artifact tooling pilot. Implemented
readers, calculations, and private writers have different verification and
support boundaries, documented by their package owners. This document's
version establishes a project baseline; package compatibility, publication,
and production support have their own release decisions.

Development focuses on EVM workflows. Add packages, integrations, network
profiles, or services for demonstrated needs. Planned framework adapters,
hosted services, and ecosystem integrations do not become supported merely
because the repository describes them.

