owners. They do not replace human contributor policy. Code and tests establish
implementation reality; they do not silently change an accepted design or
supply missing protocol evidence.

Evidence proves only its recorded scope. For deployed behavior, pinned state,
bytecode, and matching verified source take precedence over a conflicting
explanation. Preserve the evidence and resolve the maintained interpretation.
Neither this manifest nor a historical decision can make a protocol claim true.

The [historical decisions](decisions/README.md) retain original rationale,
dates, and acceptance limits. Their current rules are incorporated here and
in the delegated detailed contracts; their old bootstrap instructions do not
